Well, I had a good game going on my historic PC at home last night (PC
Nethack 1.0.4f from 1987, but the principles should be the same!), where my
priest chanced upon a spell-book of charm monster:) By level 2 I had a pet
Leprechaun who helped me rob both the shop and the shopkeepers money. Then
suddenly woosh! M'Rant the priest goes through a trapdoor, and finds
himself on level 4, which turnes out to be a bones level... and suddenly
I'm attacked by two water demons! Help!!! No wait... #cast (as you did with
spells in those days) Which spell (ab-?)
b. Hehehe, suddenly I have two pet demons!

Suddenly priest M'Rant, Prince and Lord (as I named them, seemed
appropriate names for demons) come across a liquor store, with lots of gain
level potions in it. I later go back to level 2 to rob the armour store
there, and go back to level 4. M'Rant is now level 12 with 94 Hp at level
4, which isn't half bad! Then it's time to descend to level 5... I drop
most of my stuff (? explanation follow), and try to descend only wielding a
two-handed sword, wearing crystal plate armour (creme de la creme in those
days) and a cursed ring I can't get off.

Now, if any of you have played NH1.0.4f, you'll know it had a *sligthly*
irritating bug. The first time you enter level 5, you had to carry *very
little* stuff, or else the dungeon collapsed...say no more!

"M'Rant-P killed by a panic on level 5". AAAAAAAARGH!!!  Can't believe it
happened while carrying so little stuff!



Anyway, if you Charm those demons, I'm sure you can leash 'em too!
(Wouldn't know if you can charm demons in NH3.1.3, though, never tried.)
